          "distinct": false,
          "id": "81c8ce49254a141e47eeedea5b0e68c627aadf82",
          "message": "feat(core): Kani proofs — inline-id round-trip + id-partition disjointness (sq-sqtk2.2) [SONNET-4.6] (#1480)\n\nAdd three PROVED (complete-domain) Kani harnesses to `kani_proofs` in\n`crates/sparq-core/src/dict.rs`. Spec: research/mechanized-proof-program.md §3.3 C-1.\n\nNew harnesses (pure integer arithmetic; CBMC exhausts the full bit-vector\ndomain — no unwind bound needed):\n\n  • inline_id_round_trip            — for every v in [0, INLINE_MAX],\n                                      inline_id_of_int(v) returns Some(id)\n                                      with is_inline(id) true and\n                                      id - INLINE_BASE == v exactly.\n                                      Domain: complete 30-bit space.\n  • inline_id_out_of_domain_is_none — for every i64 v < 0 or v > INLINE_MAX,\n                                      inline_id_of_int(v) returns None.\n                                      Domain: complete i64 complement.\n  • id_partition_disjoint           — the four u32 id regions (NO_ID {0},\n                                      dict [1,INLINE_BASE), inline\n                                      [INLINE_BASE, INLINE_BASE+INLINE_MAX],\n                                      local-vocab) are pairwise disjoint AND\n                                      exhaustive over all 2^32 values.\n                                      Domain: complete u32.\n\nStructural change: the module gate is widened from\n`#[cfg(all(kani, feature = \"mmap\"))]` to `#[cfg(kani)]` so the new\nnumeric harnesses run without the mmap feature. The existing mmap validator\nharnesses are individually guarded with `#[cfg(feature = \"mmap\")]` — they\nremain semantically identical (compiled-code equivalence under kani+mmap).\n\nMutation spot-check (in-worktree, documented): changing NO_ID from 0 to 1\nmakes id_partition_disjoint fail on the exhaustiveness assertion (id=0 is\nuncovered) — kani RED confirmed; constant reverted.\n\nHARNESS-ONLY: zero changes to runtime dict logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-04T17:14:15Z",
          "tree_id": "881b444d2b880c3df51c78d8292ca6a1eb794023",
          "url": "https://github.com/sparq-org/sparq/commit/81c8ce49254a141e47eeedea5b0e68c627aadf82"
