          "distinct": true,
          "id": "397ce99058776f1c12482fcbaeb256e394ac69e5",
          "message": "feat(site): register the SPARQL logic-bug paper in the factory registry (sq-gum8.9) [SONNET-4.6] (#1501)\n\nRegisters `sparql-logic-bugs` (site/papers/sparql-logic-bugs.typ, merged #1496) in\npapers.ts and wires three deterministic, canonical evidence records into\npaper-evidence.json so the paper is findable on the /papers route.\n\nRegistry entry:\n- slug: sparql-logic-bugs\n- family: A (Systems/DB)\n- status: draft  (campaign pending — bead sq-gum8.11)\n- venue: ISSTA 2027 first; PVLDB Vol 20 rolling / FSE 2027 second\n\nEvidence keys wired (all canonical, all traced to committed test constants):\n- metamorph.selftest_oracles = 3  (TLP + NoREC + differential, oracle_self_tests.rs)\n- metamorph.selftest_seeds   = 50 (generated_cases_hold_on_pristine_sparq, 0..50)\n- metamorph.grammar_exclusion_seeds = 200 (generated_predicates_respect_the_exclusion_list, 0..200)\n\nCampaign keys (confirmed/reported/rejected) are NOT wired — they are pending bead\nsq-gum8.11 and are shown as explicit PLACEHOLDERs in the .typ.\n\nsparq-engine-systems (sq-gum8.8) is NOT registered here: its .typ does not exist\nyet (sq-gum8.8 is still open), and build-papers.mjs hard-fails on a missing source.\n\nHonesty gate: 41 evidence records (33 canonical, 8 indicative) — passed.\nBuild-boundary scan: 7 papers + paper-evidence.json — passed.\nLint: clean. Static export: /papers/sparql-logic-bugs present in out/.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-04T22:46:33Z",
          "tree_id": "98f70c6a82ceddbe5356117366b439a31a2d1af7",
